Subject: [PATCH 1/3] NOTE-v1.md: the counting dichotomy's credit corrected --
 proposed for your key

"The dichotomy is Macindoe's, published in [1]" was not right, and the
sentence is ours. Upper half: Rozier 1991 (Singularite 2(5), Theoreme
p. 8, Lemme 4 p. 11), explicit in Simons-de Weger 2005 (Lemma 7,
Lemma 14, Theorem 3(d)), finiteness for each m also Brox 2000; [1]'s
Theorem 4.5 named as a rederivation by another route, with SdW's m equal
to [1]'s p exactly. Lower half: Rozier p. 11's optimality remark over
real tuples, SdW p. 69's expectation, Halbeisen-Hungerbuhler 1997's
proof in the cycle-length parameter (Lemma 5, p. 230); what is [1]'s is
the integer, all-rotations, bounded-slack realization in the block
parameter. The located obstruction keeps its quotation and gains its
credit (HH 1997 p. 238; SdW p. 69). Four references added, [5]-[8].
Nothing in the note's argument changes. Letter: rounds/R19-macindoe.md
section 1.
